---
// LocalStack · Lesson 1 — container, credentials, awslocal, first verify.
// Registered: nav.js, README (CI), hub card (done with the topic).
import Lesson from "../../../../layouts/Lesson.astro";
const titlePt = "LocalStack 1 — o primeiro comando";
const titleEn = "LocalStack 1 — the first command";
const titleFallback = "LocalStack 1 — o primeiro comando";
const bodyClass = "lang-pt";
const viewport = "width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0";
const assets = [
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/style.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/dark.css\" />",
	"<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../assets/i18n.css\" />",
	"<script src=\"../assets/i18n.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/nav.js\" defer></script>",
	"<script src=\"../assets/reading-ui.js\" defer></script>",
];
---
<Lesson
	titlePt={titlePt}
	titleEn={titleEn}
	titleFallback={titleFallback}
	bodyClass={bodyClass}
	viewport={viewport}
	assets={assets}
>
	<Fragment is:raw>
    <article class="lesson">
      <header class="hero">
        <span class="eyebrow">⬡ LocalStack · Lição 1 · Fácil</span>
        <h1>
          <span data-lang="pt">O par perfeito: LocalStack + <code>awslocal</code></span
          ><span data-lang="en">The perfect pair: LocalStack + <code>awslocal</code></span>
        </h1>
        <p class="lead">
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Em 10 minutos: seu container responde, seu CLI aponta para ele e
            você prova isso com <strong>um comando de verificação</strong>.
            Tudo grátis, tudo descartável.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >In 10 minutes: your container answers, your CLI points at it, and
            you prove it with <strong>one verification command</strong>. All
            free, all disposable.</span
          >
        </p>
      </header>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">1</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">O modelo mental: uma região falsa dentro do Docker</span
        ><span data-lang="en">The mental model: a fake region inside Docker</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >LocalStack é um <strong>emulador do AWS rodando num único processo
          Docker</strong>. Cada serviço da AWS (S3, Lambda, SQS…) escuta num
          endpoint local. Para o cliente, é como se existisse
          <code>us-east-1</code> na sua máquina.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >LocalStack is an <strong>AWS emulator running in a single Docker
          process</strong>. Each AWS service (S3, Lambda, SQS…) listens on a
          local endpoint. To the client, it is as if
          <code>us-east-1</code> existed inside your machine.</span
        >
      </p>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <div class="card">
          <h3><code>:4566</code></h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >O <strong>edge port</strong>: todos os serviços atrás de uma
              única porta.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              >The <strong>edge port</strong>: all services behind a single
              port.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3><code>test / test</code></h3>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt"
              >Credenciais <strong>fictícias</strong> — LocalStack não valida
              o que você manda.</span
            ><span data-lang="en"
              ><strong>Mock</strong> credentials — LocalStack does not validate
              what you send.</span
            >
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="callout warn">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Free tier (Community) cobre S3, Lambda, SQS, SNS, DynamoDB, API
          Gateway v1, IAM, CloudWatch Logs… <strong>RDS, ECR e API GW v2 são
          pagos</strong> — este curso evita depender deles.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >The free (Community) tier covers S3, Lambda, SQS, SNS, DynamoDB,
          API Gateway v1, IAM, CloudWatch Logs… <strong>RDS, ECR and API GW v2
          are paid</strong> — this course avoids depending on them.</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <span data-lang="pt">Fontes:</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Sources:</span>
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/getting-started/installation/">instalação</a>
        ·
        <a href="https://www.localstack.cloud/pricing-comparison">cobertura por plano</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">2</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Suba o container e instale o CLI local</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Start the container and install the local CLI</span>
      </h2>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Se você já instalou o LocalStack, pule o primeiro bloco. Se não,
          <strong>um <code>docker run</code> resolve</strong> — sem compose,
          sem licença.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >If you already installed LocalStack, skip the first block. If not,
          <strong>one <code>docker run</code> does it</strong> — no compose,
          no license.</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code><span class="c"># 1 — subir o container (pule se já está rodando)</span>
docker run -d --name localstack \
  -p 4566:4566 -p 4510-4559:4510-4559 \
  localstack/localstack

<span class="c"># 2 — o CLI que aponta sozinho para localhost:4566</span>
pip install awscli-local          <span class="c"># fornece `awslocal`</span>

<span class="c"># 3 — o CLI oficial da AWS, se ainda não tiver</span>
pip install awscli                <span class="c"># fornece `aws`</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout key">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><code>awslocal</code> é um wrapper fino do <code>aws</code> que
          <strong>já injeta <code>--endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566</code>
          e credenciais falsas</strong>. Guarde o <code>aws</code> puro para a
          AWS real.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><code>awslocal</code> is a thin wrapper around <code>aws</code> that
          <strong>already injects <code>--endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566</code>
          and mock credentials</strong>. Keep plain <code>aws</code> for real
          AWS.</span
        >
      </div>
      <p class="cite">
        <a href="https://pypi.org/project/awscli-local/">awscli-local (PyPI)</a> ·
        <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/aws/connecting/aws-cli/">conectando o AWS CLI</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">3</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Desafio (fácil): prove que está vivo</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Challenge (easy): prove it is alive</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="card">
        <h3>
          <span data-lang="pt">Passos</span><span data-lang="en">Steps</span>
        </h3>
        <ol>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Confirme o container:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Confirm the container:</span>
            <code>docker ps --filter name=localstack</code>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Crie as credenciais falsas no ambiente:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Export the mock credentials:</span>
            <pre class="block"><code>export AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test
export AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=test
export AWS_DEFAULT_REGION=us-east-1</code></pre>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Chame o STS (quem sou eu?):</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Call STS (who am I?):</span>
            <code>awslocal sts get-caller-identity</code>
          </li>
          <li>
            <span data-lang="pt">Liste as regiões… sem sair do lugar:</span
            ><span data-lang="en">List regions… without leaving the spot:</span>
            <code>awslocal ec2 describe-regions --query "Regions[].RegionName" --output text</code>
          </li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <p>
        <span data-lang="pt"
          ><strong>Verificação</strong> — o <code>sts</code> deve responder
          exatamente isto:</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          ><strong>Verify</strong> — the <code>sts</code> call must return
          exactly this:</span
        >
      </p>
      <pre class="block"><code>awslocal sts get-caller-identity
<span class="c"># esperado / expected:</span>
<span class="s">{
    "UserId": "AKIAIOSFODNN7EXAMPLE",
    "Account": "000000000000",
    "Arn": "arn:aws:iam::000000000000:root"
}</span></code></pre>
      <div class="callout tip">
        <span data-lang="pt"
          >Se der <code>Connection refused</code>: o container não está de pé
          — <code>docker start localstack</code> e espere o healthcheck.</span
        ><span data-lang="en"
          >If you get <code>Connection refused</code>: the container is not up
          — <code>docker start localstack</code> and wait for the healthcheck.</span
        >
      </div>

      <h2 class="section">
        <span class="num">4</span
        ><span data-lang="pt">Recupere sem pistas</span
        ><span data-lang="en">Retrieve without clues</span>
      </h2>
      <div class="grid cols-2">
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Qual porta serve todos os serviços?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Which port serves every service?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>4566</code> — <span data-lang="pt">o edge port</span><span data-lang="en">the edge port</span>.</p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">Quais credenciais o LocalStack espera?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">What credentials does LocalStack expect?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><span data-lang="pt">Qualquer par — o usual é <code>test</code>/<code>test</code>.</span><span data-lang="en">Any pair — the convention is <code>test</code>/<code>test</code>.</span></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt"><code>awslocal</code> injeta o quê por você?</span
            ><span data-lang="en"><code>awslocal</code> injects what for you?</span>
          </summary>
          <p><code>--endpoint-url=http://localhost:4566</code></p>
        </details>
        <details class="card">
          <summary>
            <span data-lang="pt">RDS está no plano grátis?</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Is RDS in the free tier?</span>
          </summary>
          <p>
            <span data-lang="pt">Não — Community não inclui RDS, ECR nem API GW v2.</span
            ><span data-lang="en">No — Community excludes RDS, ECR and API GW v2.</span>
          </p>
        </details>
      </div>

      <footer class="lesson-foot">
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt">Fonte primária:</span
          ><span data-lang="en">Primary source:</span>
          <a href="https://docs.localstack.cloud/getting-started/installation/"
            >LocalStack · Installation</a
          >
        </div>
        <a class="next-card" href="0002-s3-cli.html"
          ><span class="lbl"
            ><span data-lang="pt">Próxima lição</span
            ><span data-lang="en">Next lesson</span></span
          >
          <div class="t">
            <span data-lang="pt">S3 pelo CLI — buckets, objetos e site →</span
            ><span data-lang="en">S3 via CLI — buckets, objects and a site →</span>
          </div></a
        >
        <div>
          <span data-lang="pt"
            >Algo não ficou claro? Pergunte ao agente — ele é seu
            professor.</span
          ><span data-lang="en"
            >Anything unclear? Ask the agent—your teacher.</span
          >
          · <a href="../../../index.html">⬡ Hub</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </Fragment>
</Lesson>
